chg":"Across 135 complete years: Meridian's average low has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.08\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.15 to \u22120.01), about \u22121.1\u00b0F since 1890. Meridian's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.25\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.19 to +0.31), about +3.3\u00b0F since 1890. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1985, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.57\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.17 to +0.98) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.44\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.05 to +0.83). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 1 of 12 months; January and April fell. Highs rose in 11 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Meridian has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Meridian's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.47 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.04 to +0.89), about +6.3 inches since 1890. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 57.0 inches a year. The wettest year was 1973 (79.03 in); the driest, 1914 (34.92 in). Meridian almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.8 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 3 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}